      'dbfish.guide.intro': 'Everything worth knowing before you cast a line: unlock, levels, fishing spots, weather, and the highest-value catches on the island.',
      'dbfish.guide.rules': '<strong>🎣 Three rules to remember:</strong> ❶ fishing unlocks at DG Lv.2 via Vanya &nbsp; ❷ the 83 species split across River / Lake / Sea &nbsp; ❸ sell fish above 125G and cook the rest',
      'dbfish.guide.g1.h': '🎣 Unlock &amp; your first rod',
      'dbfish.guide.g1.p': 'Reach DG Lv.2 and the mentor Vanya visits you automatically, gifts you a fishing rod, and unlocks Fishing — your first production hobby.',
      'dbfish.guide.g2.h': '📈 Fishing level 1–10',
      'dbfish.guide.g2.p': 'Level up by catching fish. Many rare species are gated behind higher levels — Arctic Char and Bluegill need Lv.10, Huchen needs Lv.9.',
      'dbfish.guide.g3.h': '🎯 Reading the shadows',
      'dbfish.guide.g3.p': 'Shadow size hints at the catch: S / M / L for common fish, <strong>Golden</strong> for rare high-value species, Blue for special spawns.',
      'dbfish.guide.w.h3': 'Where to fish',
      'dbfish.guide.river.h': '🏞️ Rivers &amp; ponds',
      'dbfish.guide.river.p': 'Shallow River (Barbel), Tranquil River (Burbot &amp; Salmon), Giantwood River (Huchen) and Rosy River each hold their own specialty catches.',
      'dbfish.guide.lake.h': '🌿 Lakes',
      'dbfish.guide.lake.p': 'Meadow Lake is the best beginner spot (Goldfish, Smelt, Butterfly Koi). Forest Lake (Bass, Arctic Char), Suburban Lake (Crucian Carp) and Hot Spring Mountain Lake (Bluegill) round out the set.',
      'dbfish.guide.sea.h': '🌊 Sea &amp; ocean',
      'dbfish.guide.sea.p': 'The Fishing Village dock is the top daily sea spot (Salmon, Sardine). Whale Sea, Zephyr Sea (Beltfish), East Sea and Old Sea each hold unique catches.',
      'dbfish.guide.wst.h3': 'Weather · season · time',
      'dbfish.guide.weather.h': '🌦️ Weather',
      'dbfish.guide.weather.p': 'Rainy and rainbow days unlock rare spawns — the Golden King Crab appears <strong>only</strong> in rainbow weather. Clear days favor many sea fish.',
      'dbfish.guide.season.h': '🍂 Season',
      'dbfish.guide.season.p': 'Most fish in Heartopia are available year-round — season is rarely the limiting factor. Weather and time of day matter far more; check the specific conditions in the database before you head out.',
      'dbfish.guide.time.h': '🌙 Time',
      'dbfish.guide.time.p': 'Some fish only bite at night (Catfish, Eel) or at dusk; others only in daylight (Pufferfish, Rainbow Trout).',
      'dbfish.guide.hv.h3': '💰 High-value targets',
