      'dbinsects.guide.intro': 'Everything worth knowing before you swing a net: unlock, tools, hot spots, weather windows, and the rarest insects on the island.',
      'dbinsects.guide.rules': '<strong>🦋 Three rules to remember:</strong> ❶ bug-catching unlocks at DG Lv.8 via Naniwa &nbsp; ❷ the 67 species split across Forest / Flower Field / Hot Spring Mountain &nbsp; ❸ most rare insects only appear in specific weather — time your hunts',
      'dbinsects.guide.g1.h': '🦋 Unlock &amp; your first net',
      'dbinsects.guide.g1.p': 'Pick Bug-catching with a hobby expansion ticket (DG Lv.8) and the mentor Naniwa — at the town center — sets you up with a bug net. It\'s a collection hobby, not a money-maker, so unlock Cooking first.',
      'dbinsects.guide.g2.h': '🛠️ Nets &amp; inflatable traps',
      'dbinsects.guide.g2.p': 'Buy bug nets and inflatable insect traps from Naniwa\'s shop. Traps passively lure exclusives like the Sulkowsky\'s Morpho, while you actively net the rest.',
      'dbinsects.guide.g3.h': '🎯 Approach slowly &amp; read the weather',
      'dbinsects.guide.g3.p': 'Equip your net and creep up on insects — moving too fast spooks them. Check the weather first: many butterflies spawn only on clear days, and rainbow weather unlocks several exclusives.',
      'dbinsects.guide.w.h3': 'Where to hunt',
      'dbinsects.guide.flower.h': '🌸 Flower Field',
      'dbinsects.guide.flower.p': 'The richest bug biome — butterflies (Peacock, Purple Emperor, Mother of Pearl), bees and flower beetles all cluster here. Best on clear days.',
      'dbinsects.guide.forest.h': '🌲 Forest &amp; Forest Island',
      'dbinsects.guide.forest.p': 'Night hunters should head here — the Hercules Beetle (400G), stag beetles and moths appear on tree trunks after dark. Forest Island adds the Alpine Longhorn Beetle in rainbow weather.',
      'dbinsects.guide.mountain.h': '♨️ Hot Spring Mountain &amp; elsewhere',
      'dbinsects.guide.mountain.p': 'Mantises, jewel scarabs and dragonflies dot Hot Spring Mountain, the Fishing Village, Suburbs and your Homestead — sweep these spots to fill the encyclopedia.',
      'dbinsects.guide.wst.h3': 'Weather · season · time',
      'dbinsects.guide.weather.h': '🌦️ Weather',
      'dbinsects.guide.weather.p': 'Rainbow weather unlocks several exclusives — the Rainbow Stag Beetle, Crimson Marsh Glider, Alpine Longhorn Beetle and Cerulean Carpenter appear <strong>only</strong> then. Clear days favor butterflies; rain brings out dragonflies.',
      'dbinsects.guide.season.h': '🍂 Season',
      'dbinsects.guide.season.p': 'Insects are spring, summer and autumn only — none spawn in winter. Summer is the busiest season, with most beetles and butterflies active.',
      'dbinsects.guide.time.h': '🌙 Time',
      'dbinsects.guide.time.p': 'Butterflies and bees fly by day; moths, fireflies and the Hercules Beetle come out at night. Dusk and dawn catch the crepuscular species like the Mourning Cloak.',
      'dbinsects.guide.hv.h3': '💰 High-value targets',
      'dbinsects.guide.hv.intro': 'The insects worth a special trip — check the conditions before you head out.',
