      'beginner.week1.r6.unlock': '🦋 Bug-catching',
      'beginner.week1.r7.action': 'Stabilize loop + prepare for mid-game',
      'beginner.week1.r7.unlock': 'Co-op building',
      'beginner.week1.note': 'By Day 5-7 you want stable Cooking at 2-3 stars plus wheat production kicking in. Your actual progress depends mainly on your farming scale and cooking efficiency.',
      'beginner.res.eyebrow': 'Resource management',
      'beginner.res.h2': 'What is worth spending on, and what is not?',
      'beginner.res.intro': 'The game has three core resources: Wishing Stars (scarce), gold (earnable), and time (finite). Each has priorities — spend wisely and you get twice the results for half the effort.',
      'beginner.res.star.h3': '⭐ Wishing Star spending priority',
      'beginner.res.star.t1.h': '🥇 Top priority: bag &amp; storage expansion (first 5 times)',
      'beginner.res.star.t1.p': 'The first 5 bag expansions (+10 slots) and storage expansions (+50 slots) each cost only &lt;strong&gt;10 Wishing Stars&lt;/strong&gt; (normally 25 — a 60% discount). This is the best investment in the game — bag space directly affects gathering and fishing efficiency. Buy them from NPC Ka Ching (across from plot 8 in the northwest suburbs). In total you need &lt;strong&gt;100 stars = +50 bag slots +250 storage slots&lt;/strong&gt;. From the 6th purchase it jumps to 25 stars each, so stop buying after the discount ends.',
      'beginner.res.star.t2.h': '🥈 Second priority: hobby unlocks &amp; Cooking upgrades',
      'beginner.res.star.t2.p': 'Fishing (auto at Lv.2) and Gardening (auto at Lv.3) cost no Wishing Stars. Cooking (Lv.5, via a hobby expansion ticket) is the first real decision — and a must-pick. Later, bug-catching (Lv.8) and bird-watching (Lv.11) each need a ticket. &lt;strong&gt;The higher your Cooking level, the better your high-star odds — the same ingredients earn 50-100% more.&lt;/strong&gt;',
      'beginner.res.star.t3.h': '🥉 Third priority: functional buildings &amp; furniture',
      'beginner.res.star.t3.p': 'Extra stoves (each additional stove runs one more dish at a time), more farmland, and functional storage furniture. These directly boost your earning power — this is "spend money to make money" investing. &lt;strong&gt;More stoves mean you cook several dishes at once — going from one to four stoves quadruples how much you cook in the same time.&lt;/strong&gt;',
      'beginner.res.star.t4.h': '💡 Emergency uses &amp; places to never spend',
      'beginner.res.star.t4.p': '&lt;strong&gt;Emergency:&lt;/strong&gt; a Wishing Star does not cash out — one star buys a colourful skyrocket, a one-shot consumable with no resale value (the "resell for 1,100G" tip you will see elsewhere is unsupported). Save stars for permanent upgrades.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;❌ Never spend on:&lt;/strong&gt; speeding up crop growth (2 hours is not worth 1 star), buying base ingredients (you get them free from farming/fishing/gathering), pure decoration (advanced build mode is a Settings → Gameplay toggle — hold off until you have the materials), or speeding up pet/hobby progress',
      'beginner.res.gold.h3': '💰 Gold spending priority',
