      'beginner.dg.sources.r4.freq': 'Each activity',
      'beginner.dg.sources.r4.badge': 'Secondary',
      'beginner.dg.sources.r5.source': 'Gathering/exploring',
      'beginner.dg.sources.r5.amount': 'Very low',
      'beginner.dg.sources.r5.freq': 'Each discovery',
      'beginner.dg.sources.r5.badge': 'Passive',
      'beginner.dg.path.h3': '⚡ Fastest path DG 1→5',
      'beginner.dg.path.t1.h': 'DG 1→2 (~30 min)',
      'beginner.dg.path.t1.p': 'Finish the tutorial + 2-3 villager quests. Auto-unlocks Fishing.',
      'beginner.dg.path.t2.h': 'DG 2→3 (~1 day)',
      'beginner.dg.path.t2.p': 'Finish the rest of the day\'s villager quests (5 total). Find Blanc to unlock Gardening.',
      'beginner.dg.path.t3.h': 'DG 3→4 (~1 day)',
      'beginner.dg.path.t3.p': 'On day 2 complete all 5 quests + bonus medals from farming/fishing.',
      'beginner.dg.path.t4.h': 'DG 4→5 (~1 day)',
      'beginner.dg.path.t4.p': 'On day 3 complete 5 quests + cooking produces lots of medals. Earn your hobby expansion ticket!',
      'beginner.dg.path.summary': '&lt;strong&gt;Summary: the fastest players reach DG 5 in 2 days; a normal pace is 3 days.&lt;/strong&gt;',
      'beginner.dg.tips.h3': '🚀 6 tips to level faster',
      'beginner.dg.tips.t1.h': '① Never miss the 5 daily quests',
      'beginner.dg.tips.t1.p': 'This is the biggest source of contribution medals. If you miss even one day of all 5, your DG progress is pushed back a full day. Make accepting quests the first thing you do each login.',
      'beginner.dg.tips.t2.h': '② Stockpile common quest items in advance',
      'beginner.dg.tips.t2.p': 'Keep in storage: potatoes ×10, wheat ×10, blueberry jam ×5, strawberry jam ×5, fish and chips ×5, and various fish ×5. When a quest arrives you can hand it in instantly instead of rushing to farm/fish/cook. <strong>Grow multiple crop types to maximize quest coverage.</strong>',
      'beginner.dg.tips.t3.h': '③ Cooking — the top earner, and a request shortcut',
      'beginner.dg.tips.t3.p': 'Cooking is the strongest money-maker early on, and many villager requests ask for cooked dishes — so batch-cooking common ones lets you clear those medal-granting requests instantly. &lt;strong&gt;Cooking does not award medals by itself; medals come from the 5 daily resident requests, main/side quests, and the weekly board at Lv.13.&lt;/strong&gt;',
      'beginner.dg.tips.t4.h': '④ Prioritize the main story',
      'beginner.dg.tips.t4.p': 'Main quests reward far more medals than dailies and push your progress permanently. When a main-quest icon appears, complete it first — it is a one-time, non-repeatable chunk of experience.',
      'beginner.dg.tips.t5.h': '⑤ Star quality boosts gold — not medals',
      'beginner.dg.tips.t5.p': 'A higher hobby level raises your crit rate, so you land more ★★/★★★ results. Star quality raises the sale price — it does not grant medals. &lt;strong&gt;Medals only come from the 5 daily resident requests, main/side quests, and the weekly board at Lv.13; cooking and star ratings never generate them.&lt;/strong&gt;',
      'beginner.dg.tips.t6.h': '⑥ Do not skip seemingly useless quests',
      'beginner.dg.tips.t6.p': 'Some quests look low-reward (e.g. only 1,000G), but they all grant contribution medals. Medal value cannot be measured in gold — &lt;strong&gt;every quest is one step of DG progress&lt;/strong&gt;, and skipping any of them delays unlocking new features.',
      'beginner.dg.ref.h3': '📋 DG level quick reference (beginner relevant)',
