      'money.raw.crop.note': 'Wheat is highlighted because it is the one crop worth planting against its gold-per-hour — 25 recipes consume it. Otherwise: tomatoes and pineapples if you are farming for cash, strawberries if you want Strawberry Jam, and <strong>never turn grapes or cacao beans into jam or sauce</strong> — both lose over a thousand gold a batch.',
      'money.daily.villager.p1': 'Villagers post requests that pay gold on top of <strong>Wishing Stars and contribution medals</strong>. The medals are the part that matters most — they gate your Development Guild level, and DG level is what unlocks gardening tiers, free storage expansions and new hobbies.',
      'money.daily.villager.p2': 'Requests fall into a handful of shapes: deliver an item, catch a fish, forage something, cook a dish, or supply building materials. Because they can ask for almost anything, the cheapest way to clear them is breadth — a few plots of several crops rather than one field of the same thing.',
      'money.daily.villager.p3': '<em>We previously listed a quest count, a reset time and a gold payout per quest. None of them held up when we went looking for a source, so they are gone.</em>',
